+## Key Design Decisions
+
+### Local embedded SQLite registry index
+
+Each kiosk builds and queries its own SQLite index from validated registry snapshots. This gives predictable serial-number lookups without a running service or runtime network access. An on-site HTTPS directory and a managed search service were rejected because both would make registry lookups dependent on connectivity that the kiosks do not have; the managed service would also introduce recurring cost and credential management without a current need for richer search. Snapshot validation and index rebuilding remain private registry concerns, and the certificate-facing lookup result remains independent of the storage backend.
+
 ## Tenets
 
 - All serial-number lookup SHALL complete using files on the kiosk; no runtime network access is permitted.
